 5.5 resigned as Black after 60 moves. Opus 5.5 led by 3.7 points after move 8, then gave it back with G4 at move 9 and C5 at move 11, falling to -6.0. A series of large losses on the left edge, with B6 at move 21 the worst at 9.8 points, pushed the deficit past 20 points, and it never came back under 9.", "moments": [{"turn": 9, "text": "Opus 5.5 held a 3.7-point lead and played G4, which lost 4.2 points and dropped the lead to -0.5. The engine preferred E4, in the gap between Black's two stones in the centre."}, {"turn": 11, "text": "C5 lost 5.4 points and turned a roughly level game into -6.0. The engine wanted E8. After this Black was behind for the rest of the game."}, {"turn": 21, "text": "B6 was the worst move of Opus 5.5's game, losing 9.8 points and dropping the score from -8.5 to -18.3. The engine's choice was B8. White's B5 followed and the left side slipped away from Black."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "The 12k answered with B4, which lost 10.1 points and brought the score from -26.0 back to -15.9. The engine's choice was E8. It was one of several large swings the 12k gave back in the middle game."}, {"turn": 30, "text": "A8 was the 12k's worst move, losing 14.6 points and moving the score from -27.6 to -13.1. The engine preferred C8. The 12k still held a large lead afterward."}, {"turn": 37, "text": "D9 lost 6.6 points and the lead went from -9.9 to -16.6, while the engine would have played H3. This was one of several late moves where Opus 5.5 lost 5 to 7 points and the deficit grew, while the 12k lost 6.9 points on moves 36 and 38."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a board passed on stdin and flood-fills each group to print its stones and liberties, and the other commands only read or append to games.md (a game log with notes). Nothing chooses, ranks, or looks ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}